<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBQA-AI37-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-AI37-002" ;
  triage:title "PyGraftSession::mailbox_work_counts duplicates the 14-arg ReadQuery::new(...) construction already in read()" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-graft-python/src/lib.rs: `fn read(&self)` (line 351) and `fn mailbox_work_counts(&self)` (line 393), one method below it, both construct `ReadQuery::new(home_dir, current_dir, self.caller.agent().clone(), None, self.caller.team().cloned().expect(\"validated caller team\"), ReadSelection::All, false, <true|false>, None, None, None, None, None, None)` with the same 14 positional arguments, differing only in the ReadSelection::All-scope-vs-count boolean flag, then chain `.map_err(atm_error)?.with_caller_chat_id(self.caller.chat_id().cloned())` identically. Recommend extracting a shared `build_read_query(...)` helper to avoid the 14-arg duplication and reduce the risk of the two call sites drifting when ReadQuery's constructor signature changes." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "boundary_tightening" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:blockingCurrentMerge false ;
  triage:note "Remediation: extract a shared build_read_query() helper on PyGraftSession used by both read() and mailbox_work_counts() to eliminate the duplicated 14-arg ReadQuery::new(...) construction." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AI37-QA-1 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-29T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-29T07:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-AI37-002/read> ,
    <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RBQA-AI37-002/mailbox-work-counts> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/phase-AI/feature-pAI-s37-hermes-recovery-summary> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAI-s37-hermes-recovery-summary" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

